00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:50.590
Prices over-react to news when the people trading a lag can only chase it, and they under-react

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:52.550
when private information is still spreading.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:58.470
A 1999 paper in the Journal of Finance builds that sequence with two groups of boundedly

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.790
rational agents, news watchers and momentum traders.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:07.230
Each news watcher sees some private information and fails to pull other news watchers information

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.170
out of prices.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.890
Gradual diffusion leaves the quote lagging in the short run.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:15.870
That lag is what lets momentum traders profit by trend chasing.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:21.770
If they can run only simple, univariate strategies, the attempt at arbitrage produces over

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.450
reaction at long horizons.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:28.750
One market can show both mistakes in that order, and the same setup throws off several

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.250
other distinctive implications.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:35.910
The size measurement sits in a 2006 journal of finance paper on the disposition effect,

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:41.930
the tendency to ride losses and realize gains, mutual fund-holding supply a reference purchase

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:47.490
price for individual stocks, and the test asks whether that tendency induces under-reaction

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.430
to news and return predictability.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:54.270
On a news date, some holders are ahead of that reference price, and some are behind.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:59.250
Drift after the announcement is most severe when those capital gains and the news have

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:04.850
the same sign. How large the drift is depends on the gains or losses holders are sitting on that

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:10.530
day, not on the headline alone. An event-driven strategy based on this effect yields monthly

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:15.930
alphas of over 200 basis points. That figure was measured in stocks and fund holdings.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:22.670
It is not a method for any contract, and it is not a reason to take a side. A 2014 paper in

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:27.750
management science finds an overshoot, and it locates the overshoot in who trades together.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:35.310
Mutual funds heard into stocks with consensus sell-side analyst upgrades and heard out of stocks with consensus downgrades.

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:42.230
Recommendation changes pull that hurting harder on downgrades and harder among managers with greater career concerns.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:49.430
Those managers look incentivized to follow analyst information and more inclined to heard on negative stock information,

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.950
given the reputational and litigation risk of holding losers.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:53.150
users.

