00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:28.930
A 1992 paper in the Journal of Finance is the dispute and it cuts the analyst channel down.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:34.210
Forecasts underreact to recent earnings, a feature consistent with properties of the naive

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:40.430
seasonal random walk that Bernard and Thomas in 1990 hypothesize underlie post-earnings

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:45.530
