00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:50.370
to explain the size of the drift. Half is not zero, and it is not the whole drift.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:56.750
Extreme forecasts studied by debaunt and thalar in 1990 cannot be viewed as overreactions to earnings,

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:01.710
and they are not clearly linked to the stock price overreactions in debaunt and thalar,

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:09.010
1985 and 1987, and in Chopra, Lakana Shock, and Ritter. Analyst behavior is at best

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:12.810
only a partial explanation for stock price under reaction to earnings,

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:19.030
