00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:24.230
lag is at most half an account of the earnings drift and possibly no account of the longer

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:30.550
over reactions. Options split the question by the shape of the news. A 2001 paper in the Journal

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:35.150
of Finance looks at how that market reacts to changes in the instantaneous variance of the

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:40.570
underlying asset. Investors there under react to individual daily changes in that variance.

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:45.590
They overreact to periods of mostly increasing or mostly decreasing daily changes.

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:50.850
They underreact to a current daily change preceded mostly by changes of the opposite sign,

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:54.510
and overreact when the preceding changes mostly share the sign.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:59.870
That third finding can reconcile the first two, and the paper says it fits well-established

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:00.850
